.Dd April 2, 2026
.Dt GALE 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm gale
.Nd isolated package management for developers
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Ar command
.Op Ar args ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is a package manager for developer CLI tools.
It fetches verified artifacts from an index, pins
them in a lockfile, and activates them through
atomic generation snapshots.
.Pp
Packages are declared in
.Pa gale.toml .
Install and update resolve the index.
Sync activates the v2 lock and does not rewrite it.
A package that is not in the index is an error.
A v1 lock migrates with
.Cm fetch-adopt .
.Pp
.Nm
supports both global packages
.Pq installed to Pa ~/.gale
and per-project environments
.Pq via direnv integration .
.Sh COMMANDS
.Ss Package Management
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm install Ar pkg Ns Op @ Ns Ar ver
Install a package from the index.
Stages
.Pa pkg/fetch/ ,
writes
.Pa gale.toml
and a v2 lock, then swaps
.Pa current .
Use
.Ar pkg@ver
to install a specific version.
Use
.Fl -index Ar dir
to resolve against a local index checkout.
.Pp
.Dl $ gale install jq
.Dl $ gale install go@1.26.1
.It Cm remove Ar pkg
Remove a package from the store and
.Pa gale.toml .
.Pp
.Dl $ gale remove htop
.It Cm sync
Activate every package the v2 lock names.
It fetches missing trees and rebuilds the generation.
It does not write
.Pa gale.lock .
Typically invoked automatically by direnv.
.Pp
Use
.Fl -if-needed
to sync only when the last sync did not complete on the
current
.Pa gale.toml
and
.Pa gale.lock .
A sync that completed is a silent no-op.
A sync that failed is retried at most once every ten
minutes, and each activation in between prints one line
naming the packages still missing.
The direnv hook uses this flag; a sync run by hand ignores
it and always does the work.
.Pp
.Dl $ gale sync
.Dl $ gale sync --if-needed
.It Cm update Op Ar pkg Ns Op @ Ns Ar ver ...
Update packages from the index to the latest version, or
to a specific version with
.Ar pkg@ver .
Use
.Fl -index Ar dir
to resolve against a local index checkout.
.Pp
.Dl $ gale update
.Dl $ gale update jq@1.8.1
.It Cm list Op Fl -scope Ar all|shared|host Op Fl g | Fl p | Fl a
List packages declared in
.Pa gale.toml
with their versions.
Use
.Fl -scope
to filter shared and host overlay entries
.Pq default Li all .
Use
.Fl g
to list global packages from inside a project,
.Fl p
to force project scope, or
.Fl a
to list both with section headers.
.Pp
.Dl $ gale list
.Dl $ gale list --scope host
.Dl $ gale list -a
.It Cm gc Op Fl -force
Remove unused package versions from the store and
old generations.
Keeps versions referenced by any
.Pa gale.toml ,
by the active generation, and by every generation above
the active one, in the global scope, the project scope,
and every project recorded in
.Pa ~/.gale/projects ,
so a gc run from one directory cannot sweep versions
another project still links.
.Pp
The generations above the current one are the branch a
rollback abandoned.
Their directories are never removed automatically, so the
versions they link are never swept either: a generation
whose packages are gone cannot be rolled onto.
The next rebuild allocates above the highest number;
keep-2 then prunes history below the new cutoff.
Generations below the current one are removed, and the
versions only they linked are reclaimed \(em that is how a
superseded revision goes after
.Cm update .
Registry entries whose project directory has vanished
are pruned on each real run.
Each build of a dirty tree installed with
.Ic install Fl -path
keeps its own store directory, so a development loop
accumulates them.
.Nm Cm gc
is how they are reclaimed, once no generation links
them.
With
.Fl -dry-run ,
also lists the registered projects that contributed
retention.
.Pp
Refuses to sweep, naming the project, when a registered
project still exists but its config or its active
generation cannot be read.
An unreadable project is not proof that its packages are
unreferenced; a down network mount is the usual cause.
A project that is genuinely gone reads as absent and
sweeps normally.
Use
.Fl -force
to sweep anyway.
.Pp
When gc rebuilds a generation it takes the versions from
that scope's lockfile, so the rebuild cannot put a version
the lock does not name on PATH.
A scope whose lockfile is present and cannot be read is
refused;
.Fl -force
rebuilds it without the lock.
.Pp
.Dl $ gale gc --dry-run
.Dl $ gale gc
.Dl $ gale gc --force
.El
.Ss Inspection
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm info Ar pkg Op Fl g | Fl p
Show package metadata: version, store path, scope,
and config path.
For uninstalled packages, shows registry information.
With
.Fl g ,
read only the global
.Pa gale.toml \(em
this is how to view a global entry that a project
.Pa gale.toml
shadows.
.Pp
.Dl $ gale info jq
.Dl $ gale info jq -g
.It Cm which Ar binary Op Fl g | Fl p
Show which installed package provides a binary and
print its full path.
Scope flags select which generation's
.Pa current/bin
is searched.
.Pp
.Dl $ gale which jq
.Dl jq@1.8.1
.Dl /Users/you/.gale/pkg/jq/1.8.1/bin/jq
.It Cm outdated Op Fl -recipes Ar dir Op Fl -no-refresh Op Fl g | Fl p
Show packages that have newer versions available in
the registry.
Pass
.Fl -recipes
to resolve against a local recipes checkout instead, or
.Fl -no-refresh
to skip the automatic tap refresh.
.Pp
.Dl $ gale outdated
.Dl jq 1.7.1 -> 1.8.1
.It Cm doctor Op Fl -check-registry
Check the gale installation for common problems:
PATH configuration, store integrity, stale generations,
host-overlay shadows, and lib farm drift.
It also reports the states that block a rebuild: a lockfile
in a schema this build cannot use, a store directory whose
.Pa .gale-deps.toml
cannot be read, and two declared packages shipping the same
executable name.
It also reports, without failing, the man pages and root-level
files more than one declared package provides.
Those are not arbitrated: the first package in sorted order
provides the file, and removing one provider is the only way to
change which.
On macOS it fails when an installed binary in the active
generation's closure carries an
.Pa @rpath
dependency reference that none of its own rpath entries
resolves.
Such a binary aborts under
.Xr dyld 1
on the next exec; rebuild it with
.Cm gale install --build Ar pkg .
The check is skipped on other platforms.
A scope whose last sync did not complete is reported the same
way, naming the packages that failed.
Run
.Cm gale sync
to retry them at once; an automatic retry waits out the
ten-minute interval.
Doctor does not rebuild generations, delete store directories,
or re-sign binaries. The remedy it prints is a command the
user runs.
.Pp
.Dl $ gale doctor
.Dl $ gale doctor --check-registry
.El
.Ss Generation Management
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm generations Op Fl g | Fl p
List all generations.
.Sy *
marks the active one,
.Sy +
a generation above it left by a rollback.
Scope flags select the project or global generation
directory.
.Pp
.Dl $ gale generations
.Dl $ gale generations -g
.It Cm generations rollback Op Ar N Op Fl g | Fl p
Switch to a previous generation.
Defaults to the previous generation (current \- 1).
Atomic symlink swap, same as install/sync.
Refuses a generation whose symlinks do not all resolve,
naming it, and leaves the current one active.
An incomplete generation is one whose store versions are
gone; activating it would put broken entries on PATH.
Rebuild from config with
.Cm sync ,
or rerun
.Cm gc Fl -force
after it falls below current.
.Pp
.Dl $ gale generations rollback
.Dl $ gale generations rollback 3
.El
.Ss Project Environment
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm init
Create a
.Pa gale.toml
and
.Pa .envrc
in the current directory, setting up direnv integration.
.Pp
.Dl $ gale init
.It Cm env Op Fl -vars-only Op Fl g | Fl p
Print shell export commands to activate the environment.
Use
.Fl -vars-only
to print only
.Ic [vars]
exports from
.Pa gale.toml .
Use
.Fl g
to opt into global vars and PATH from inside a project.
.Pp
.Dl $ eval "$(gale env)"
.Dl $ eval "$(gale env -g)"
.It Cm shell
Open an interactive shell with the project environment
activated.
.Pp
.Dl $ gale shell
.It Cm run Ar cmd Op Ar args ...
Run a command in the project environment.
Syncs packages if
.Pa gale.toml
has changed.
.Pp
.Dl $ gale run go test ./...
.It Cm hook direnv
Print the
.Fn use_gale
shell function for
.Pa ~/.config/direnv/direnvrc .
.Pp
.Dl $ gale hook direnv >> ~/.config/direnv/direnvrc
.El
.Ss Index
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm lint Ar file.toml ... Op Fl -base Ar old.toml
Validate one or more index files.
A document with a top-level
.Ic versions
table is an index file.
The filename stem must match
.Ic package.name .
A source recipe is not an index document.
.Fl -base
compares one index file to a previous document
and refuses append-only violations.
.Pp
.Dl $ gale lint index/j/just.toml
.Dl $ gale lint --base old.toml index/j/just.toml
.It Cm admit
Record an index artifact from a local archive.
Extracts with Gale's installer path, computes
.Ic tree_digest ,
and prints a TOML fragment.
Does not write the store, lock, or
.Pa gale.toml .
.Pp
.Dl $ gale admit --archive just.tar.gz --name just --version 1.56.0 --os darwin --arch arm64 --url https://github.com/casey/just/releases/download/1.56.0/just.tar.gz --file just:bin/just:755
.El
.Ss Supply Chain Security
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm verify Op Ar pkg Op Fl g | Fl p
Recompute each locked fetch tree digest and
compare it to the v2 lock.
Does not talk to GHCR.
A v1 lock has no tree_digest.
Scope flags select which lockfile to read.
.Pp
.Dl $ gale verify jq
.El
.Ss Shell Completion
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm completion bash | zsh | fish | powershell
Generate a shell completion script.
.Pp
.Dl $ gale completion zsh > ~/.zfunc/_gale
.El
.Sh FLAGS
.Ss Global Flags
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl v , -verbose
Verbose output.
.It Fl n , -dry-run
Show what would happen without making changes.
Applies to all mutating commands:
.Cm install , remove , sync , update , gc .
.It Fl q , -quiet
Suppress non-essential status output.
Warnings and errors still print.
.It Fl -plain
Disable color, progress bars, and step indicators.
Use when capturing output for logs or tests.
.It Fl -no-color
Disable colored output.
Same as setting
.Ev NO_COLOR
to a non-empty value.
.It Fl -error-format Ar text|json
Format top-level runtime errors.
Default
.Li text .
.El
.Ss Scope Flags
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl g , -global
Target the global
.Pa ~/.gale/gale.toml .
.It Fl p , -project
Target the project
.Pa gale.toml .
.Pp
When neither flag is set, defaults to project scope
if a
.Pa gale.toml
exists in the directory tree, otherwise global.
Applies to mutation commands
.Pq Cm install , add , remove , sync , update , switch
and to read-only commands
.Pq Cm list , info , sbom , outdated , env , which , verify , audit , generations .
.It Fl a , -all
For inventory commands
.Pq Cm list , sbom ,
list packages from both project and global
.Pa gale.toml
under
.Sq Project:
and
.Sq Global:
section headers.
Mutually exclusive with
.Fl g
and
.Fl p .
.El
.Ss Index Flag
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -index Ar dir
Resolve install, update, lock, and fetch-adopt against
a local index checkout.
The directory must be a git repository.
Uncommitted edits are invisible.
.El
.Ss Build Flags
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -debug
Build with debug flags:
.Fl O0 Fl g ,
no symbol stripping.
.It Fl -release
Build with release flags, overriding any debug setting
in the recipe or config.
.El
.Ss Output Flags
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -json
Output in JSON format
.Pq Cm sbom .
.It Fl -vars-only
Print only
.Ic [vars]
exports
.Pq Cm env .
.El
.Sh BUILD ENVIRONMENT
Build steps run in a clean shell with only essential
tools on PATH.
The following variables are set:
.Pp
.Bl -tag -width "DYLD_FALLBACK_LIBRARY_PATH" -compact
.It Ev PREFIX
Install destination directory.
.It Ev VERSION
Package version from the recipe.
.It Ev JOBS
CPU count for parallel builds.
.It Ev OS
Operating system
.Pq Li darwin , Li linux .
.It Ev ARCH
Architecture
.Pq Li arm64 , Li amd64 .
.It Ev PLATFORM
.Ev OS Ns - Ns Ev ARCH
.Pq e.g. Li darwin-arm64 .
.El
.Pp
When build dependencies are installed, additional
paths are set:
.Pp
.Bl -tag -width "DYLD_FALLBACK_LIBRARY_PATH" -compact
.It Ev LIBRARY_PATH
Library directories from dependencies.
.It Ev C_INCLUDE_PATH
Header directories from dependencies.
.It Ev PKG_CONFIG_PATH
Pkg-config directories from dependencies.
.It Ev CMAKE_LIBRARY_PATH
CMake library search path.
.It Ev CMAKE_INCLUDE_PATH
CMake include search path.
.It Ev CMAKE_PREFIX_PATH
CMake prefix path (cmake builds only, semicolon-separated).
.It Ev LD_LIBRARY_PATH
Dynamic linker path (Linux only).
.It Ev DYLD_FALLBACK_LIBRARY_PATH
Dynamic linker fallback path (macOS only).
.El
.Pp
Compiler flags default to
.Fl O2
for release builds and
.Fl O0 Fl g
for debug builds.
User-set
.Ev CFLAGS ,
.Ev CXXFLAGS ,
and
.Ev LDFLAGS
are never overridden.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Install packages and set up a project:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ gale install ripgrep bat fd
$ cd myproject
$ gale init
$ gale install go@1.26.1
$ gale install golangci-lint
.Ed
.Pp
Update every package in the manifest:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ gale update
$ gale update jq
.Ed
.Pp
Use direnv for automatic project environments:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ gale hook direnv >> ~/.config/direnv/direnvrc
$ cd myproject
$ gale init
$ direnv allow
.Ed
.Pp
Admit an artifact into a local index:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ gale admit just-1.58.0-aarch64-apple-darwin.tar.gz
$ gale lint --base old.toml index/j/just.toml
$ gale install just --index ../gale-recipes
.Ed
.Pp
Check store trees against the lock:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ gale verify jq
.Ed
.Sh CONFIGURATION
Application settings in
.Pa ~/.gale/config.toml :
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ic [build]
.Bl -tag -width "debug" -compact
.It Va debug
When true, all builds use debug flags.
Default: false.
.El
.It Ic [anthropic]
Leftover. Ignored.
.El
.Pp
The recipe registry URL is compiled in.
Leftover
.Ic [registry] url
and
.Ic [sync] parallelism
keys are ignored.
.Pp
Package declarations in
.Pa gale.toml :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
[packages]
jq = "1.8.1"
go = "1.26.1"

[vars]
GOPATH = "${HOME}/go"

[hosts.my-mac.packages]
fzf = "0.50"

[hosts.my-server.packages]
htop = "3.0"
.Ed
.Pp
Top-level
.Ic [packages]
applies on every machine.
.Ic [hosts. Ns Ar name Ns Ic .packages]
sections add machine-specific packages when the local
hostname matches
.Ar name .
Host entries override shared entries when both
declare the same package.
Leftover
.Ic [bin]
and
.Ic [hosts. Ns Ar name Ns Ic .bin]
keys are ignored.
Two packages shipping the same basename refuse the
generation. Remove one package.
The active host is
.Ev GALE_HOST
if set, otherwise the value returned by
.Xr hostname 1 .
.Pp
Use
.Fl -host Ar name
on
.Cm add , install , remove ,
and
.Cm lock
to target a host section.
.Fl -host current
expands to the current machine.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev NO_COLOR
Disables colored output when set to a non-empty value,
regardless of TTY status.
Follows the
.Lk https://no-color.org
convention.
An empty value is ignored.
.It Ev GALE_HOST
Overrides the hostname used to select
.Ic [hosts. Ns Ar X Ns Ic ]
sections in
.Pa gale.toml .
Defaults to
.Xr hostname 1 .
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "~/.gale/config.toml" -compact
.It Pa ~/.gale/gale.toml
Global package declarations.
.It Pa ~/.gale/config.toml
Application settings (API keys, registry URL).
.It Pa ~/.gale/pkg/
Package store.
One directory per package per version.
.It Pa ~/.gale/current/
Symlink to the active generation directory.
Add
.Pa ~/.gale/current/bin
to PATH.
.It Pa ~/.gale/projects
Machine-local project registry, one absolute path per
line, recorded automatically on project-scoped use.
.Cm gc
retains every registered project's pins and active
generation.
.It Pa gale.toml
Project package declarations.
.It Pa gale.lock
Lockfile with SHA256 hashes for reproducibility.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr brew 1 ,
.Xr direnv 1
